    33	READ = """# Blind reader: which of these big matters does this library hold a question on? (read-only)
    34	
    35	You are a senior hedge-fund analyst covering NVIDIA. Below are the big matters readers listed from the news of 2026-09-07 to 09-20, each with
    36	an example question, and the library of one research system as it stood on 2026-09-20: every question it held, open or closed, with its id,
    37	due day and possible answers. Systems write their questions in different styles; ignore style.
    38	
    39	For each matter choose one:
    40	- **opened**: a question the same outcome would settle, in any reasonable wording, period or date the news supports (name its id);
    41	- **narrower**: a question on part of the matter (name its id, and say whether it carries the matter's main outcome);
    42	- **broader**: the matter is folded into a wider question;
    43	- **missed**: no question on it.
    44	
    45	Do not count a reasonable alternative shape as missed: a different deadline the news itself states, or one year of a two-year matter, is
    46	"opened" or "narrower" with a note. Several questions may cover one matter: name them all.
    47	
    48	Then list the library's duplicates: two questions of the library are the same bet when the same outcome settles both and their answers
    49	cannot move apart (another year of a figure is another bet). Of such a pair, the later-opened question is the duplicate.
    50	
    51	Write one JSON object per line, and nothing else:
    52	- per matter: {{"matter": "M01", "status": "opened|narrower|broader|missed", "ids": ["..."], "main_outcome": true|false|null, "note": "<= 30 words"}}
    53	- per duplicate: {{"duplicate": "<later id>", "of": "<earlier id>"}}
    54	
    55	## The matters
    56	
    57	{matters}
    58	
    59	## Library {label}
    60	
    61	{library}
    62	"""
    63	
    64	THIRD = """# Third reader: does this question cover this matter? (read-only)
    65	
    66	You are a senior hedge-fund analyst covering NVIDIA. Two readers disagreed on whether the question below covers the matter below. A question
    67	covers a matter when the same outcome would settle both (any reasonable wording, period or date), or when it is on part of the matter and
    68	carries the matter's main outcome. Answer from the two texts.
    69	
    70	Write one JSON object and nothing else: {{"covers": true|false, "why": "<= 40 words"}}
    71	
