The exporter opened historical stores from both systems. The scorer returned a practical lead with five draws and a practical loss at exactly +10 percentage points. Both results violate the frozen rule. [build_cards.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/build_cards.py:51) · [verdict-rule.json](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/verdict-rule.json:59)

1. **Require six eligible cutoff snapshots.** The new-system path is hardcoded to the first attempt even when the judge records a successful `-redo`. Resolve the recorded successful attempt, verify all six original draws meet the timing rules, and bind their snapshots and the frozen matter list to scoring. The scorer currently checks only draws supplied to it. [mapping.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/mapping.py:95) · [run_stage_b.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_b/run_stage_b.py:89) · [score_comparison.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:101) · [Plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md:174)

2. **Validate mapping before counting.** Supply the source material A2 uses to judge alternative dates. Require one valid mapping per matter, real question IDs and valid later-to-earlier duplicate pairs. Require both named third-reader votes before calling a disagreement a split. Missing votes currently become splits, and unvalidated duplicate IDs change the distinct-bet count. [A2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/week/brief-A2.md:3) · [mapping.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/mapping.py:133) · [mapping.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/mapping.py:217)

3. **Fix the guardrails.** Keep the seeded sample and pooled denominators, exclude covering cards from the shares, and compare the 10-point threshold using integer counts. Preserve the minimum of ten unsplit decided cards per subgroup and system. Emit the required insufficient, no-answer and split counts alongside the shares. [mark_cards.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/mark_cards.py:99) · [score_comparison.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:73) · [Frozen rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/verdict-rule.json:48)

4. **Fix the cards and finish the blinding check.** The exporter labels the speaker as the publisher and drops quote continuations. Verify every archived evidence item renders in full. Use the specified shuffle seed and resolve the second blinding check’s bullet-count findings while preserving the actual outcomes and library contents. [build_cards.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/build_cards.py:34) · [Judge format](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:128) · [Card spec](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/card-spec.md:22) · [Second check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/blinding-check-codex-2.md:1)

5. **Seal debate rounds and control marks.** Independent marking passes card text only. Debate reads the latest files, so a resumed round can expose a same-round mark, and export can skip debate. Use completed prior rounds. Select plants with a distinct adjacent rung, retain the separate support confirmations, and count two explicit rejections as rejection even if the labels differ. Keep repeats outside product counts and compare both marks. [mark_cards.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/mark_cards.py:82) · [mark_cards.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/mark_cards.py:167) · [score_comparison.py](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/score_comparison.py:101) · [Frozen controls](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/stage0/verdict-rule.json:64)

